# Ledger for test/diff_compiler_prelude_shadow_census.sh (#2153, S-shadow-census-gate).
#
# One row per top-level standalone function exported from stdlib/core.mdk,
# `name|verdict`, where verdict is the CURRENT MEASURED outcome of the probe:
#
#   interface Ifc c where
#     <name> : c -> Int
#   impl Ifc Int where
#     <name> v = v
#   main = println (<name> 1)
#
# driven through `check`, `run`, and `build` (+ executing the built binary).
#
#   PASS                -- check/run/build all ACCEPT and both run's stdout
#                          and the built binary's stdout print exactly `1`
#                          (S1-PRELUDE (a): the interface method wins and the
#                          program builds, docs/spec/SHADOW-SEMANTICS.md).
#   FAIL_BUILD           -- check and run ACCEPT (run prints `1`), but build
#                          exits 1: `runtime error [E-PANIC]: unbound method:
#                          <name>` -- #2153's class, the gate this slice ships
#                          to make objectively measurable.
#   SPECIAL_RUN_REJECT   -- `println` only: shadowing `println` changes what
#                          type `main` infers to, and `run` rejects with the
#                          ORDINARY non-Unit-main W-MAIN-SHAPE exit (byte-
#                          identical to `main = 7` with no interface anywhere)
#                          -- not a shadow-resolution artifact. `build` still
#                          accepts and prints `1`, but that `1` is itself a
#                          live, filed bug (#2185: the compiler's own
#                          auto-print wrap resolving to the user's shadowing
#                          method), not a benign or expected accept. Not part
#                          of the #2153 family; kept as its own bucket rather
#                          than folded into either of the other two, per the
#                          packet's own note that `println` is special-cased.
#
# THIS LEDGER IS THE RATCHET: a PASS row that regresses to anything else is a
# gate failure, full stop -- see the gate's own header for how a name moving
# the OTHER direction (e.g. a slice 2-5 fix flipping FAIL_BUILD -> PASS) is
# handled (re-pin this row, on purpose, in that slice's own diff).
#
# Names are derived from stdlib/core.mdk at gate-run time (never hand-copied
# from #2153's issue body) -- the gate's own coverage self-audit fails loudly
# if a name here has vanished from core.mdk, or a core.mdk standalone is
# missing from this ledger (a NEW prelude function ships with no ledger row).
#
# Measured 2026-08-28 at the census gate's landing commit, cold-built binary:
# 57 standalone names, 34 PASS / 22 FAIL_BUILD / 1 SPECIAL_RUN_REJECT.  (#2153's
# issue body claimed "33 pass / 23 fail / println special" -- the ledger's
# numbers were the derived truth, one name off in each direction from the
# issue's prose count.)
#
# RE-PINNED 2026-08-28 by S-mangle-unclaim-residual (slice 2): all 22 FAIL_BUILD
# rows flipped to PASS, ON PURPOSE and in that slice's own diff, per this file's
# ratchet rule above.  The FAIL_BUILD class had ONE root cause -- the graph-wide
# definer-shadow map (`computeMangledShadowMap`) minted `core__<n> |-> <n>` for a
# USER module's interface method and CORE's own prepass consumed it unfiltered, so
# core's own `core__<n>` occurrence was marked `EMethodAt "<n>"` in a unit whose env
# has no `<n>`.  A name reached that arm only if ANOTHER prelude decl referenced it,
# which is exactly why the split was 22/34 (`marker.droppablePreludeFns`' own
# `clamp` yes / `count`,`find` no split).  Fix: `typecheck.coreShadowMapFor`.
# Current measured split: 56 PASS / 1 SPECIAL_RUN_REJECT (`println`, slice 3's).
